      "id": "PRJ-ISSUE-1",
      "severity": "high (privileged callers only)",
      "what": "POST /projects (deadline) and PATCH /projects/:id (deadline, startedAt) interpolate request values into raw SQL without escaping. Callers need admin or moderator (POST) or admin (PATCH).",
      "status": "FIXED in PRJ-06",
      "evidence": "projects/infrastructure/sql/project-raw-sets.ts and its characterization test; identical SQL text in the CRUD differential test.",
      "decision": "Fixing changes behavior (rejects or alters values that work today); needs its own approved change.",
      "fix": "deadline and startedAt now pass through esc() like every other raw field; valid date strings generate identical SQL."
    },
    {
      "id": "PRJ-ISSUE-3",
      "severity": "low (admin and moderator callers only)",
      "what": "PATCH /projects/:id/enrollments/:enrollmentId/status validates the new status with an index lookup on a plain object, so inherited keys such as toString, constructor and hasOwnProperty pass validation. The enrollment's status is then set to that string and a non-string action is handed to the activity log.",
      "status": "FIXED in PRJ-06",
      "evidence": "The original route (same lookup) and the extracted domain function behave identically in the whole-file differential test; a characterization test pins it.",
      "decision": "Needs its own approved change (use an own-property check); a fix rejects inputs the endpoint accepts today.",
      "fix": "moderationLogAction uses an own-property check and requires a string; toString, constructor etc. and non-strings now get the 400."
    },
    {
      "id": "PRJ-ISSUE-2",
      "severity": "functional bug: POST /projects returned 500 after creating (confirmed by code reading of drizzle node-postgres db.execute, which returns snake_case rows; not run against a live database)",
      "what": "POST /projects applies a follow-up raw UPDATE ... RETURNING * whenever the body carries category, projectType, exchangeSubType, accountCategory, deadline, durationType, difficulty or costType, then calls formatProject on the returned raw row. lib/db sets no snake-to-camel mapping, so if node-postgres returns snake_case columns, createdAt is undefined and formatProject throws after the row is inserted and broadcast: the client sees a 500 for a project that was created.",
      "status": "FIXED after PRJ-07",
      "evidence": "projects/domain/project.ts#formatCreatedProject builds the response from the typed insert row and adds raw columns from the UPDATE ... RETURNING row; application/projects.ts#createProject uses it. domain/project.test.ts pins the old throw and the new output."
    },
    {
      "id": "PRJ-ISSUE-4",
      "severity": "probable data-quality bug, NOT confirmed on the live database",
      "what": "project_enrollments has no unique constraint on (project, user, entity) in the Drizzle schema or any .sql file in the repo, so the bulk-enroll INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING probably never conflicts: repeating a bulk enroll likely inserts duplicate enrollment rows. Since PRJ-07 each inserted row is charged, so repeating a bulk enroll now charges again.",
      "status": "FIXED in code after PRJ-07 (no schema change)",
      "evidence": "projects/domain/bulk-enroll-plan.ts + test, projects/application/bulk-enrollment.ts; remaining risk: no unique constraint, so two concurrent identical requests can still race"
    }
  ],
